From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:29:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: apple-sio: Stop submission before draining
 callbacks

A submission that has already left vc.lock can still publish a request,
or roll its block back after an allocation failure, while the stop work
drains callbacks and releases the active descriptor. Cancel the submit
work first; the stop work queues submission again itself afterwards.
Both run on the unordered high-priority workqueue, so this cannot wait on
itself. This applies to every SmartIO DMA channel.

[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/orchard#205 (tompta1, 09038adf),
 kernel/patches/drivers/soc-apple/0043; commit message written.]

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/dma/apple-sio-dma.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/apple-sio-dma.c b/drivers/dma/apple-sio-dma.c
index aa304dc66..33a7aa430 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/apple-sio-dma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/apple-sio-dma.c
@@ -478,6 +478,13 @@ static void sio_dma_stop_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	bool busy, issued;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * A submission already outside vc.lock can still publish a request or
+	 * roll back its block after an allocation failure. Quiesce it before
+	 * draining callbacks and releasing the active descriptor.
+	 */
+	cancel_work_sync(&chan->submit_work);
+
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&chan->vc.lock, flags);
 	busy = chan->inflight;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&chan->vc.lock, flags);
